abstract = {This research is focus on the global stability of the 1D compressible isentropic micropolar fluid model characterized by viscous dependence on density under constant disturbance. p(v) = v− γ is defined as pressure and μ(v) = v− α is defined as the viscosity coefficient for some parameters (alpha ,gamma in mathbb {R}) are taken into account. The study aims to demonstrate the existence of strong solutions and analyze their large-time behavior to the Cauchy problem when subjected to large initial data and perturbed from constant state. To achieve this, the authors employ a priori assumption together with refined energy estimates under α and γ suitable certain parameter conditions conditions with the initial data taken to be sufficiently regular, in the absence of vacuum and mass concentrations. Determining the upper and lower limits about uniform-in-time on the particular volume is a crucial component of the proof.},
